# Cursor Rules for mcp-server-web-audit

- Always use strict TypeScript mode
- Never write to stdout directly; only write logs to stderr (console.error or pino)
- Every exported function must include JSDoc comments
- Keep functions under 40 lines and files under 300 lines
- Ensure SSRF validation is applied to all incoming URLs
- Run `pnpm test` and `pnpm typecheck` before committing changes
